libswirl — the SwirlOS userspace runtime
========================================

libswirl.a is the static library every SwirlOS application links against.
It is a real file on disk at /system/lib/libswirl.a, and it contains:

  - the int 0x80 syscall wrappers (open/read/write/spawn/wait/...)
  - printf and friends (vsnprintf, integer formatting)
  - string and memory helpers (memcpy, strlen, strcmp, snprintf)
  - the process entry point (_start), which calls your main()

Rebuild it from the SwirlOS source tree:  user/lib/
This directory keeps the copy that shipped with this system image.
